From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cool-retro-term-wezterm <build@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:26:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] Settings menu sliders; menu callbacks survive
 configuration reloads

InputSelector choices can carry a slider (value, min, max, step, names):
it is drawn as a segmented bar in one column after the labels, Left/Right
(h/l) move it without closing the selector (Shift: a fifth of a step) and
each change is passed to the action callback as a fifth argument.  Changes
are reported one at a time; while one is handled only the latest waits.

Callbacks created at run time (a menu opened from an event handler) only
exist in the lua context that created them.  After a configuration reload
their events went to the new context and were lost, so a menu reopened
after saving a value stopped reacting.  Callback names are now unique per
configuration generation, the last few contexts are kept (most recently
used first), and the selector, prompt and confirmation overlays emit their
event in the context that registered it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
